(S, "The inverse of which type of matrix does not exist?", ["Singular matrix", "Identity matrix", "Non-singular matrix", "Diagonal matrix with non-zero entries"], 0, "A matrix has an inverse only if its determinant is not zero. A singular matrix has determinant zero, so it has no inverse.", "A square matrix with a non-zero determinant is called non-singular or invertible.", [2725]),
